  <!-- What is FreshBooks -->
  <section class="editorial" style="padding-top:0;margin-top:0;border-top:none;">
    <p class="section-label">What is FreshBooks?</p>
    <p>FreshBooks is a cloud-based accounting and invoicing platform founded in Toronto in 2003. It now serves over 30 million people across 160 countries, but its focus has never shifted: it is built for freelancers, independent contractors, and small service-based businesses where billable time is the primary revenue driver.</p>
    <p>Unlike QuickBooks, which tries to serve everyone from sole traders to mid-size companies, FreshBooks makes deliberate tradeoffs in favour of simplicity. You get excellent invoicing, time tracking, and expense management in an interface that does not assume you have an accounting background. What you do not get is the full general-ledger depth a growing company with complex inventory or payroll needs. That tradeoff is the right one for most freelancers.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Pricing -->
  <section class="editorial">
    <p class="section-label">FreshBooks pricing in 2026</p>
    <p>FreshBooks has four plans. All prices are monthly when billed monthly; annual billing saves roughly 10%.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Price</th><th>Billable clients</th><th>Key addition</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Lite</strong></td><td>$23/mo</td><td>5</td><td>Core invoicing, time tracking, expenses</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Plus</strong></td><td>$43/mo</td><td>50</td><td>Recurring invoices, double-entry accounting, proposals</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Premium</strong></td><td>$70/mo</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Project profitability, business health reports</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Select</strong></td><td>Custom</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Dedicated account manager, lower transaction fees</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Additional team members cost $11/month per person on all plans. The 5-client cap on Lite is the most common objection to FreshBooks. If you have six active clients, you are immediately pushed to the $43 Plus tier. If you have fewer than five clients and are just starting out, Lite is genuinely good value.</p>
    <p>FreshBooks frequently runs 70 to 90% off promotions for the first three months. The full price kicks in at month four. Check the current offer on their pricing page before signing up.</p>
    <div class="cta-strip">
      <p>See current pricing and active discounts</p>
      <a href="#" class="cta-btn">Check FreshBooks pricing [AFFILIATE LINK]</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Features -->
  <section class="editorial">
    <p class="section-label">FreshBooks features breakdown</p>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">🧾</div>
        <p class="feature-name">Invoicing</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Customisable templates, automatic late-payment reminders, recurring invoices, late fees, and a client portal for online payment. You can create a professional invoice in under two minutes.</p>
        <details class="read-more" style="margin:0.75rem -1rem -1rem;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;">
          <summary>Read more</summary>
          <div class="read-more-body">
            <p>The automation is where FreshBooks earns its money. Set up a recurring invoice for a retainer client and forget about it. Configure automatic late-payment reminders and FreshBooks sends them without you touching anything. Automatic late fees can also be applied to overdue invoices.</p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> FreshBooks branding appears in invoice emails on Lite and Plus plans. The Premium plan and above remove it.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">⏱</div>
        <p class="feature-name">Time tracking</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Built into every plan. Start a timer from the web or mobile app, assign it to a client or project, and those hours populate your next invoice automatically.</p>
        <details class="read-more" style="margin:0.75rem -1rem -1rem;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;">
          <summary>Read more</summary>
          <div class="read-more-body">
            <p>This is the feature that most clearly differentiates FreshBooks from Wave and Zoho Invoice, both of which have weaker native time tracking. If you bill by the hour at all, this feature alone makes FreshBooks worth considering over the free alternatives.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">💳</div>
        <p class="feature-name">Expense tracking</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Connect your bank account or credit card and FreshBooks pulls in transactions automatically. Photograph receipts on mobile and attach them directly to invoices for reimbursement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">📁</div>
        <p class="feature-name">Project management</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Project budgets, task tracking, and team collaboration. Not a replacement for Asana or ClickUp, but covers the basics for a freelancer managing several client projects at once.</p>
        <details class="read-more" style="margin:0.75rem -1rem -1rem;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;">
          <summary>Read more</summary>
          <div class="read-more-body">
            <p>Project profitability tracking (which projects are actually making you money after time and expenses) is gated behind the Premium plan at $70/month. For most solo freelancers, the Plus plan covers everything needed.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">📱</div>
        <p class="feature-name">Mobile app</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">iOS and Android. Create invoices, start timers, capture receipts, log mileage, and check payment status from your phone. One of the better mobile invoicing experiences in the category.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">🔗</div>
        <p class="feature-name">Integrations</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">200+ integrations including Stripe, PayPal, Gusto, HubSpot, Shopify, Slack, and Google Workspace. Zapier extends the list further.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pros / cons -->
  <section class="editorial">
    <p class="section-label">Pros and cons</p>
    <div class="pros-cons-card">
      <div class="pros-cons-inner">
        <div class="pros-col">
          <p class="pc-label">Pros</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Best invoicing UX in the category</li>
            <li>Time tracking built into every plan</li>
            <li>Automatic late payment reminders and recurring invoices</li>
            <li>Solid mobile app for invoicing on the go</li>
            <li>30-day free trial, no credit card required</li>
            <li>Strong customer support (phone and chat)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cons-col">
          <p class="pc-label">Cons</p>
          <ul>
            <li>5-client cap on the $23/mo Lite plan</li>
            <li>No free plan</li>
            <li>$11/mo per additional team member</li>
            <li>Not a full accounting tool</li>
            <li>Limited VAT support for European freelancers</li>
            <li>FreshBooks branding on invoice emails on lower plans</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Is it worth it -->
  <section class="editorial">
    <p class="section-label">Is FreshBooks worth it?</p>
    <p>At $23/month for Lite, the question is whether the automation saves you enough time to justify the cost. Conservatively: automatic payment reminders save most freelancers 30 to 60 minutes per month in follow-up emails. Recurring invoices for retainer clients save another 30 minutes. Time tracking that flows directly into invoices eliminates manual hour-counting. Total saved: 2 to 3 hours per month.</p>
    <p>If your time is worth more than $8 per hour, FreshBooks Lite pays for itself in the first billing cycle. The calculus changes if you have more than 5 clients and are on a tight budget. At $43/month for Plus, you need the automation to save more than two hours a month. For most freelancers billing regularly, it does.</p>
  </section>

