          <tr><td><strong>Invoicing</strong></td><td>★★★★★</td><td>★★★★</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Accounting depth</strong></td><td>★★★</td><td>★★★★★</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Time tracking</strong></td><td>Built in (all plans)</td><td>Add-on</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Starting price</strong></td><td>$23/mo</td><td>$38/mo</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Free trial</strong></td><td>30 days</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:0.85rem;font-size:0.85rem;color:#374151;">For a freelancer whose main needs are invoicing, time tracking, and basic expense management, FreshBooks is the stronger choice. For a business needing payroll, inventory, or complex tax workflows, QuickBooks handles more.</p>
