    <p class="section-label">Frequently asked questions</p>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is FreshBooks worth it for freelancers?</summary>
        <p>Yes, for most freelancers who invoice more than a handful of clients per month. The automation saves 2 to 3 hours a month and pays for the subscription within the first billing cycle. Check the 5-client cap on Lite before signing up.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How much does FreshBooks cost per month?</summary>
        <p>FreshBooks starts at $23/month (Lite, 5 clients), $43/month (Plus, 50 clients), or $70/month (Premium, unlimited clients). Each additional team member costs $11/month. FreshBooks frequently runs intro discounts of 70 to 90% off for the first three months.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does FreshBooks have a free plan?</summary>
        <p>No. FreshBooks offers a 30-day free trial with no credit card required. If you need permanently free invoicing, Wave and Zoho Invoice are the strongest alternatives.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is the FreshBooks Lite plan limit?</summary>
        <p>The Lite plan at $23/month allows up to 5 billable clients. If you have a 6th active client, you need to upgrade to Plus at $43/month. The limit applies to active clients, not invoices — you can send unlimited invoices to your 5 clients.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is FreshBooks better than QuickBooks for freelancers?</summary>
        <p>For most freelancers, yes. FreshBooks wins on ease of use, invoicing quality, and time tracking. QuickBooks wins on accounting depth and US tax features. If your needs are invoicing and basic bookkeeping, FreshBooks is the cleaner, less expensive choice.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I try FreshBooks for free?</summary>
        <p>Yes. FreshBooks offers a 30-day free trial on all plans with no credit card required.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
